act-lite
========

act-lite parses source code with the tree-sitter grammars listed below. Each
grammar is distributed under its own license, stated here with its source and
copyright line. "registry" means the crate is fetched from crates.io at build
time; a path means the grammar is vendored in this repository with its
LICENSE file beside it. Where the grammar's LICENSE file carries no copyright
line, the line below is taken from the crate's Cargo.toml `authors` field, or
names the upstream contributors when that field is empty too.

The full license texts of these grammars and of every other crate in the
release binaries are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.

